From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Archit Gupta <archit@accelbread.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 04:37:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] pgtk: Queue redraw after updating mouse highlight

Mouse motion updates mouse-face in the Cairo backing surface, but PGTK
does not queue a GTK draw to present the change.  The highlight therefore
remains stale until unrelated redisplay, such as a cursor blink or click,
queues a draw.

Queue a draw after note_mouse_movement changes the highlighted glyph.
This makes mouse-face enter and leave updates visible immediately
(bug#80221).

* src/pgtkterm.c (motion_notify_event): Queue a draw after mouse
highlight changes.
---
 src/pgtkterm.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/pgtkterm.c b/src/pgtkterm.c
index 733c7d2..8931291 100644
--- a/src/pgtkterm.c
+++ b/src/pgtkterm.c
@@ -6027,7 +6027,12 @@ motion_notify_event (GtkWidget *widget, GdkEvent *event,
 	  last_mouse_window = window;
 	}
 
-      if (!note_mouse_movement (f, &event->motion))
+      if (note_mouse_movement (f, &event->motion))
+	{
+	  if (!buffer_flipping_blocked_p ())
+	    gtk_widget_queue_draw (FRAME_GTK_WIDGET (f));
+	}
+      else
 	help_echo_string = previous_help_echo_string;
     }
   else
